# Source packages from `R CMD build` / Build Source Package. Regenerated on
# demand, so there is never a reason to track one.
*.tar.gz

# Working notes, deliberately untracked: a scratchpad rather than documentation,
# and it named unannounced products. Kept on disk, out of the repo.
_TODO.md

# Debris from deliberately-failed test runs (the disable-and-recheck habit).
# testthat writes the broken copies here; they are never part of the package.
tests/testthat/_problems/

# The other half of that debris, and it is a file rather than a directory, which
# is why the rule above never caught it. testthat writes it when a run fails and
# deletes it when one passes, so a copy was committed by accident and then
# vanished the next time the suite was green.
tests/testthat/testthat-problems.rds

# Benchmark output. The harness in `bench/` is tracked; what it measures is
# machine-specific and regenerated on demand, so the numbers are not.
bench/*.csv
